I eventually observed that much of the time that I used up a "oLS I was
already in such trouble the crowd surrounding me killed me again
anyways.  Then I observed that either a better AC or better attack or
better playing strategy would have saved me without using the "oLS in
the first place.  So I ended up prefering better AC (which should mean
shield), better attack (which means classes that can either dual wield
or use attack spells drop the shield) and better strategy (oh right,
learn from my mistakes.  I wish that worked for the classic "death by
typo").

Reflection saves more of my characters from one-shot deaths than life
saving does from crowds of nasties.  Magic resistance saves more of my
characters from battles of armor depleting attrition than life saving
does from crowds of nasties.  In both cases the resistance helps on the
second attack but life saving does not.

There's also the classic Nethack strategy of - That didn't work in this
game.  Time to start a new character and try something else.  Like why I
got into that mess in the first place was often about equipment choices
five levels up not about details of what I did on that level.


